{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "name": "right_beaker_pour_into_left_tube",
  "description": "Right arm picks the beaker, left arm picks the tube (independent sub-graphs, run concurrently). Carry-out is staggered like the return: the right beaker departs for its work pose first and the left tube departs no earlier than 8 s after the right arm set off. Then the right beaker tips into the tube mouth and returns upright. On the way back the left arm departs first and the right arm departs 5 s later, so the two returns overlap. Finally both arms return to the calibrated initial pose together. Assumes both jaws are already open: run prepare_open_grippers first, because this graph never opens a gripper.",
